{"base_rate":0.7702205882352942,"brier":0.1892610294117647,"bss":-0.06938715035799548,"bss_hi":0.08825775495210413,"bss_lo":-0.21800706658741284,"country":"IS","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve"],"ece":0.15492647058823522,"ess":403.8774135458697,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Reykjavik</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Reykjavik rain forecast is cannot beat its own climatology, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>90%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(3%), there is still roughly a <b>50%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 544 days, 2024-05-01 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nREYKJAVIK, 2.9 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score -0.07, ranked 15 of\n15 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(15&ndash;15) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>3%</td><td class='num'><b>50%</b></td><td class='num'>54</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>36%</td><td class='num'><b>53%</b></td><td class='num'>55</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>71%</td><td class='num'><b>67%</b></td><td class='num'>52</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>89%</td><td class='num'><b>63%</b></td><td class='num'>57</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>90%</b></td><td class='num'>326</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 5 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Reykjavik\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"68.09555555555556,355.03703703703707 184.21709090909087,209.76181818181908 309.54423076923075,81.0 371.4452631578947,30.771929824561425 410.92496932515337,18.0 410.92496932515337,21.349693251533722 371.4452631578947,94.63157894736844 309.54423076923075,172.00000000000003 184.21709090909087,295.9636363636364 68.09555555555556,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"101.63970588235293\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"101.63970588235293\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"68.09555555555556,200.0 184.21709090909087,190.0727272727273 309.54423076923075,136.99999999999997 371.4452631578947,152.10526315789474 410.92496932515337,55.96319018404904\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 3%&amp;#10;It rained 50% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 54 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"68.09555555555556\" cy=\"200.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 36%&amp;#10;It rained 53% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 55 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"184.21709090909087\" cy=\"190.0727272727273\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 71%&amp;#10;It rained 67% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 52 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"309.54423076923075\" cy=\"136.99999999999997\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 89%&amp;#10;It rained 63% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 57 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"371.4452631578947\" cy=\"152.10526315789474\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 90% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 326 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"410.92496932515337\" cy=\"55.96319018404904\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(77%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p class=\"muted\">Not enough days in this city's record to split the year into four and still say anything defensible about each part. The split is shown only where it is supported.</p>\n"},"lat":64.1466,"lon":-21.9426,"n":544,"n_cities":15,"name":"Reykjavik","offset_days":-1,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.14,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.028518518518518523,"n":54,"obs":0.5,"sig":true},{"hi":0.5820000000000002,"lo":0.14,"mean":0.35654545454545444,"n":55,"obs":0.5272727272727272,"sig":true},{"hi":0.8,"lo":0.5820000000000002,"mean":0.710576923076923,"n":52,"obs":0.6730769230769231,"sig":false},{"hi":0.9520000000000002,"lo":0.8,"mean":0.885438596491228,"n":57,"obs":0.631578947368421,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.9520000000000002,"mean":0.996963190184049,"n":326,"obs":0.8957055214723927,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":2.9,"rank":15,"rank_hi":15.0,"rank_lo":15.0,"reliability":0.03804418635368823,"resolution":0.025568068572086357,"slug":"reykjavik","station":"REYKJAVIK","timezone":"Atlantic/Reykjavik"}